Haakon Studebaker wrote:

> What symbol is used for an open door? Most times I find myself wanting
> to use the quick goto command but I don't know the symbol for an open
> door. 

It is what a user of pure ASCII graphics might have expected:
either '-' or '|' for horizontal or vertical open doors, resp.
Unfortunately that's true for horizontal or vertical walls, too.

There are additional special symbols in {ibm,dec,mac}_graphics[],
namely 0xfe, 0xe1, and 0xee, resp. Using the Windows executable with
IBMGraphics option I did not succeed to enter that character with
neither nhdefkey.dll nor the default altkeyhandler.

But with telnet on NAO it works. Of course typing several ALT-2-5-4
I wouldn't consider to yield a quick goto command.

